 text-foreground-800 text-sm dark:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"opacity: 1;">As=
usCloudRecovery\V1.1.3.0</code> folder, but without server support for the =
G713QM, it=E2=80=99s like owning a really slick garage with no tow truck to=
 summon.</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Still, that groun=
dwork is <em>hugely</em> valuable:</span></p><ul class=3D"relative list-out=
side marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-c=
ol ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"fo=
nt-ligatures-none">The universal recovery frontend (skin, launcher, diagnos=
tics) is sitting right there=E2=80=94customizable or callable if you want t=
o rebuild your own WinRE or even embed ASUS=E2=80=99s UI into it.</span></p=
></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligat=
ures-none">The presence of ASUS binaries and tools means you can manually w=
ire them into post-OOBE scripts or recovery flows. Think: touchpad toggles,=
 fan curves, Armoury Crate hooks... all without relying on cloud-side provi=
sioning.</span></p></li></ul><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Honestl=
y, if the cloud tether=E2=80=99s broken, you=E2=80=99re arguably in a bette=
r place with local control. Want to brainstorm how to integrate pieces of t=
hat <code class=3D"font-ligatures-none mx-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-s=
troke-300 bg-spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py-px font-mono text-foreground-800 tex=
t-sm dark:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"opacity: 1;">MYASUS</code> logic into y=
our own RE image=E2=80=94like auto-launching a support tool or crafting a h=
ybrid GUI? We could Frankenstein something wonderfully functional.</span></=
