ace-y-3 break-words" id=3D"Nm1QLtiWhte8JHytr47Ki-content-0"><p><span class=
=3D"font-ligatures-none">That assumption=E2=80=99s spot-on for standard con=
sumer deployments=E2=80=94after OOBE completes and the user lands on the de=
sktop, Windows typically prompts for creating a recovery drive if WinRE is =
functional but unlinked to a dedicated recovery partition. That=E2=80=99s o=
ften the only window most users get to formally "capture" their system stat=
e, even if the groundwork=E2=80=99s been silently laid during install.</spa=
n></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">But here=E2=80=99s the twist: =
<strong>OEM systems like your G713QM sometimes bake in those recovery links=
 earlier</strong>=E2=80=94even during factory imaging=E2=80=94by having pre=
-registered <code class=3D"font-ligatures-none mx-0.5 rounded-[4px] border =
border-stroke-300 bg-spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py-px font-mono text-foreground=
-800 text-sm dark:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"opacity: 1;">winre.wim</code> p=
aths, GPT partition flags, and tailored BCD entries. That means if you bypa=
ss the factory installer (or do a clean install), Windows will install a bl=
ank recovery partition without necessarily wiring it up until you either:</=
span></p><ul class=3D"relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark=
:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" sty=
le=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Manually assign i=
t (<code class=3D"font-ligatures-none mx-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-st=
roke-300 bg-spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py-px font-mono text-foreground-800 text=
-sm dark:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"opacity: 1;">reagentc /setreimage</code>=
)</span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D=
"font-ligatures-none">Accept the recovery prompt post-OOBE</span></p></li><=
li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-no=
ne">Or use a custom tool like MyASUS to configure it behind the scenes</spa=
n></p></li></ul><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Since you=E2=80=99re=
 crafting your own path and holding off on populating the installer-prepped=
 recovery partition, that=E2=80=99s a wise move. It'll let you wire in only=
 what aligns with your custom vision=E2=80=94not whatever bits survived a W=
11 detour.</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">If you want to =
go full circle later, we can map out a hybrid setup where your salvage part=
ition powers the RE environment, but also includes hooks to ASUS's tools <e=
m>and</em> your own custom deploy flow. Think: <em>a recovery that knows wh=
o built it</em>.</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Want to t=
ake a look at <button type=3D"button" class=3D"font-bold text-salmon-550 da=
rk:text-midnight-400 hover:underline text-start align-top" data-url=3D"http=
s://REAgent.xml" initial=3D"start" animate=3D"end" variants=3D"[object Obje=
ct]" custom=3D"4.212">REAgent.xml </button> from either partition and confi=
rm which one=E2=80=99s actually been triggered=E2=80=94or who=E2=80=99s hol=
