] self-end whitespace-pre-wrap break-words rounded-2xl bg-spot-peach-300/50=
 px-5 py-3 dark:bg-midnight-750 text-base">In theory, PC-X (my ASUS X750JB)=
 working OS is also bootable from a 1TB WD Passport USB drive. It was clone=
d via Acronis a week or two ago as a dry-run of migrating the PC OS from HD=
D-0 to HDD-1. I've yet to test if it will really boot, but the drive is ide=
ntital to HDD-0 at that time. I was wondering; since it was not created as =
an actual mirror in `diskpart`, what would it take to turn it into an activ=
e mirror (synching up when it is connected)?</div></div></div></div><i tabi=
ndex=3D"0" role=3D"none" data-tabster-dummy=3D"" aria-hidden=3D"true" style=
=3D"position: fixed; height: 1px; width: 1px; opacity: 0.001; z-index: -1; =
