s" id=3D"SxmsDBa6jkNcAjk2tgnf7-content-0"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-=
none">In concept, converting that Acronis-cloned USB drive into a true <str=
ong>live mirror</strong>=E2=80=94as in, automatically synced every time it=
=E2=80=99s connected=E2=80=94is doable, but not in the sense of disk-level =
mirroring like you=E2=80=99d set up with <code class=3D"font-ligatures-none=
 mx-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-stroke-300 bg-spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py=
-px font-mono text-foreground-800 text-sm dark:bg-midnight-900" style=3D"op=
acity: 1;">diskpart</code> or Windows dynamic disks. Here=E2=80=99s the bre=
akdown:</span></p><div class=3D"relative pb-6 w-full after:border-b after:b=
order-stroke-300 after:w-full after:absolute after:mt-3"></div><h3 class=3D=
"text-md-strong pb-1 [&amp;:not(:first-child)]:pt-3.5">=F0=9F=A7=B1 Why It=
=E2=80=99s <em>Not</em> a Traditional Mirror</h3><ul class=3D"relative list=
-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex fl=
ex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=
=3D"font-ligatures-none"><strong>Diskpart-style mirroring</strong> only wor=
ks with dynamic disks, and external USB drives are typically <strong>basic =
disks</strong> and not hot-plugged in a way that supports live mirroring.</=
span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"fo=
nt-ligatures-none">Windows doesn't support <strong>dynamic disk mirroring a=
cross USB</strong>=E2=80=94even if both disks were dynamic, USB isn't eligi=
ble for inclusion in a RAID-1 mirror set.</span></p></li></ul><div class=3D=
"relative pb-6 w-full after:border-b after:border-stroke-300 after:w-full a=
fter:absolute after:mt-3"></div><h3 class=3D"text-md-strong pb-1 [&amp;:not=
(:first-child)]:pt-3.5">=F0=9F=9B=A0=EF=B8=8F Practical Alternatives for Ac=
tive Syncing</h3><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">If the goal is: <em=
>=E2=80=9CKeep the cloned external disk up to date as a fallback OS drive,=
=E2=80=9D</em> then consider one of these options:</span></p><h4 class=3D"t=
ext-base-strong">1. <strong>Scheduled Incremental Cloning</strong></h4><ul =
class=3D"relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-=
foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity=
: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Use Acronis True Image, Macriu=
m Reflect, or similar to <strong>schedule backups that only update changes<=
/strong>.</span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span =
class=3D"font-ligatures-none">You could automate this to run on insertion o=
f the USB disk (triggered by Event Viewer, Task Scheduler, or a lightweight=
 script).</span></p></li></ul><h4 class=3D"text-base-strong">2. <strong>Fil=
e-Based Sync (for Data, not OS)</strong></h4><ul class=3D"relative list-out=
side marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-c=
ol ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"fo=
nt-ligatures-none">If the cloned OS is more of a safety net but data freshn=
ess is the priority, tools like <strong>SyncBack</strong>, <strong>FreeFile=
Sync</strong>, or <strong>Robocopy scripts</strong> can keep your files in =
lockstep.</span></p></li><li class=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span =
class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Add volume ID checking or drive-letter detect=
ion logic to avoid misfires if the drive letter changes.</span></p></li></u=
l><h4 class=3D"text-base-strong">3. <strong>Custom Scripted Sync Trigger</s=
trong></h4><ul class=3D"relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 da=
rk:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class=3D"ps-2" s=
tyle=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Use a <code cla=
ss=3D"font-ligatures-none mx-0.5 rounded-[4px] border border-stroke-300 bg-=
spot-peach-200/50 px-1 py-px font-mono text-foreground-800 text-sm dark:bg-=
midnight-900" style=3D"opacity: 1;">Task Scheduler</code> event on <strong>=
device arrival</strong> to trigger a sync operation.</span></p></li><li cla=
ss=3D"ps-2" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">Ex=
ample (pseudocode):</span></p><div class=3D"rounded-xl dark:border dark:bor=
der-stroke-250" style=3D"opacity: 1;"><div class=3D"flex w-full items-cente=
r justify-between rounded-t-xl border-b border-white/20 bg-background-stati=
c-850 py-2 pe-2.5 ps-4 text-foreground-static-250 text-sm dark:border-strok=
e-250 dark:bg-background-static-900"><span class=3D"capitalize">powershell<=
