</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">As for <strong>Macrium Re=
flect Free</strong>, it used to offer indefinite usage for non-commercial p=
urposes with fairly generous features, including VSS-based backups and diff=
erential imaging. That said, the free edition was officially discontinued f=
or new updates back in mid-2023. If you already have a copy tucked away, it=
=E2=80=99s still perfectly usable=E2=80=94but it won=E2=80=99t get feature =
or security updates anymore. Worth checking which version you=E2=80=99ve go=
t if you do decide to revisit it.</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligature=
s-none">Since Acronis already covers your base image strategy, your best be=
t for lightweight sync or incremental options=E2=80=94especially for bootab=
le clones=E2=80=94might just be <strong>manually scheduled</strong> Acronis=
 jobs. If you're curious, I can help configure one-time or recurring tasks =
for "connect-and-update" behavior that respects your OS structure without g=
oing RAID-fantasy on USB.</span></p><p><span class=3D"font-ligatures-none">=
